  "notes": "Refers to the complete destruction of all microorganisms including bacteria, viruses, and spores. Stricter than {殺菌|さっきん} (disinfection), which only reduces the number of pathogens.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {滅菌|めっきん}{処理|しょり}: sterilization treatment\n- {滅菌|めっきん}{済|ず}み: sterilized (done)\n- {高圧|こうあつ}{滅菌|めっきん}: autoclave sterilization\n- {滅菌|めっきん}ガーゼ: sterile gauze\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {殺菌|さっきん}: disinfection, pasteurization — kills or reduces harmful bacteria but does not eliminate all microorganisms\n- {消毒|しょうどく}: disinfection, sanitization — a broader term for cleaning to remove pathogens; used in everyday contexts like hand sanitizing\n- {除菌|じょきん}: removing bacteria — commonly seen on household cleaning products; less technical than {滅菌|めっきん}",
